# Build context for the web image (Dockerfile). The build stage does
# `COPY package.json package-lock.json` + `npm ci`, then `COPY . .` +
# `npm run build`, so the context only needs what Vite/SvelteKit actually
# read: src/, static/, and the config files (svelte.config.js, vite.config.ts,
# tsconfig.json, package*.json).
#
# Two paths must NOT be excluded:
#   - nginx.conf: the runtime stage COPYs it straight from the context.
#   - static/:    adapter-static copies it into build/.

# Installed deps and build output — regenerated inside the image
node_modules
build
.svelte-kit

# VCS and CI metadata
.git
.github

# Planning, agent, and docs history — never read by the build. This is the
# big win: .planning alone is ~7.3 MB of what was a ~12 MB context.
.planning
.claude
docs

# The api image builds from its own context (docker-compose*.yml: ./server)
server

# Tests: vite.config.ts's `test.include` is read by vitest, never by
# `vite build`
tests

# Docker/compose files are not consumed inside the image
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml

# Secrets. `.env.*` also covers .env.example, which the build does not read
# (the API base URL comes from the VITE_API_BASE_URL build arg).
.env
.env.*
